# Production build config — loaded automatically by `vite build` (NOT by
# `vite dev` / `npm run dev`, so local dev via run.py is unaffected).
#
# An EMPTY VITE_BACKEND_URL makes every API call relative (/agent, /config,
# /mermaid, /thread/*), so the deployed SPA talks to the SAME ORIGIN that serves
# it (the Caddy edge) — no CORS, no hardcoded host. config.ts still falls back to
# http://localhost:8000 in dev mode where this file is not loaded.
VITE_BACKEND_URL=
